# Kinetics Observer — shared working brief

Common ground for anyone (human or agent) picking up this work. Written 2026-09-02.
It records the goal, the two pipelines, how evaluation and the covariance search work, the
conventions that have already caused wrong conclusions, and the current blocker.

Companion documents:
- `KINETICS_INVESTIGATION.md` — the running investigation log (findings, ablations, verdicts).
- `~/Documents/ResearchNotes/Thesis/Manuscript/Sections/Appendix/Appendix_Analyt_Jacs.tex` — the
  analytical Jacobian derivations the C++ implements.

---

## 1. The goal

Show that **MCKineticsObserver (KO)** — a centroidal EKF fusing IMU, kinematics and contact
force/torque through a visco-elastic contact model — beats the **RI-EKF baseline** (Hartley's
invariant EKF, run as the standalone `InEkfLogParser`) on the relative-pose metrics, across 13
mocap datasets, without giving the KO an advantage the baseline does not get.

Metrics, all as `KO / RI-EKF` ratios (lower is better, 1.0 = parity):

| metric | what it is |
|---|---|
| `trans_perc` | relative translation error, % of the sub-trajectory length |
| `yaw` | relative yaw error, deg |
| `tilt` (`gravity`) | relative roll/pitch error, deg |
| `vel` | RMS error of the observer's **own estimated local linear velocity** state — not a finite difference of its position. Included so a tuning cannot buy pose accuracy by becoming sluggish. |

**Ground rules for fairness.** Anything the RI-EKF also consumes must be changed on both sides or
not at all. Sensor calibration is off-limits as a tuning knob. A model correction that fixes a
genuine physical error is fair even when it is KO-only (the RI-EKF has no mass term at all, and
uses force only for contact detection); a *tuning knob* only one side gets is not.

### Datasets (13)

```
HRP5_MultiContact_1..4          HRP5P,  5 ms, 3 contacts (2 feet + LeftHandCloseContact)
HRP5P_LongWalk                  HRP5P,  2 ms, 1697 s, 282 m walked inside a ~6x5 m box
KO_TRO2024_RHPS1_1..5           RHPS1,  5 ms
KO_TRO_2024_RHPS1_SLIPPAGE_1..3 RHPS1,  5 ms
```

Per-project settings live in `Projects/<name>/projectConfig.yaml` (`predefined_sublengths`,
`Body_vel_eval`, `EnabledRobot`, `EnabledBody`).

---

## 2. The two pipelines

Both start from the same recorded `raw_data/controllerLog.bin` and end in the same rpg metric code.
They differ in **how the observer is executed**.

### Pipeline A — "the routine" (`scripts/routine_scripts/mainRoutine.sh`)

Runs the observer **inside mc_rtc**, as a live observer.

```
raw_data/controllerLog.bin
  └─ mc_rtc_ticker --no-sync --replay-outputs -e -l controllerLog.bin
       Passthrough controller; ObserverPipelines instantiates MCKineticsObserver
       alongside MCValinor, MCKineticsObserverFG, the HartleyIEKF plugin.
       Contact detection, kinematics and wrenches computed live from the robot model.
  └─ output_data/logReplay.bin -> logReplay.csv -> lightData.csv
  └─ resampleMocapAndExtractPose.py   (mocap reference)
     crossCorrelation.py              (time sync, by cross-correlating local linear velocity)
     matchInitPose.py                 (frame alignment)
  └─ finalDataCSV.csv     -> KO_position_*, Hartley_*, Mocap_*, Control_*
  └─ plotAndFormatResults.py -> output_data/evals/<Observer>/stamped_traj_estimate.txt
                              -> output_data/formattedMocap_Traj.txt   (ground truth)
  └─ computeMetrics.sh -> rpg analyze_trajectory_single.py
                       -> evals/<Observer>/saved_results/*/relative_error_statistics_<sub>.yaml
```

### Pipeline B — "the replay" (`scripts/kinetics_eval.py`)

Runs the **bare `KineticsObserver` C++ class** standalone (no mc_rtc), fed inputs A recorded.
This is the **fast tuning loop**.

```
prepare:
  raw_data/controllerLog.bin
    └─ mc_rtc_ticker again (regenerate_full_log) -> kinetics_eval/logReplay_full.bin
       (needed because the routine lightens logReplay.bin, stripping MEKF_* debug channels)
    └─ bin_to_rosbag_kinetics.py  (+ kinetics_bag_common.py)
         reads MEKF_inputs_*, MEKF_measurements_*, debug_contactKine_*, MEKF_initialState_*
         writes a ROS 2 bag:  KineticsConfiguration (once) + KineticsInput (per tick)
    └─ kinetics_eval/reference/{mocap,riekf,mocap_velocity,riekf_velocity}.txt  from finalDataCSV
run:
  test_kinetics_replay.launch.py -> kinetics_offline_replay node
    └─ kinetics.txt / kinetics_centroid.txt / kinetics_velocity.txt
    └─ analyze() -> same rpg code vs reference/mocap.txt -> summary.csv
```

| | A (routine) | B (replay) |
|---|---|---|
| observer runs | inside mc_rtc | standalone node, bare estimator |
| kinematics/wrenches | computed live | replayed verbatim from A's log |
| contact detection | Schmitt trigger, live | replays the `isSet` flag A recorded |
| cost (LongWalk) | full re-tick, 30 min+ | ~7 min |
| covariance changes | edit live mc_rtc YAML | overlay file, mc_rtc untouched |

**They must agree.** B consumes exactly what A's observer consumed, so the same estimator with the
same config must reproduce A's trajectory. Verified 2026-09-02 on HRP5_MultiContact_4 with both
built from one revision: position 0.0137 mm mean / 0.112 mm max, and the rpg metrics agree to 0.04%.

### Useful commands

```bash
# prepare one project (re-ticks only if logReplay_full.bin is missing; move it aside to force)
.venv/bin/python scripts/kinetics_eval.py --projects <NAME> prepare --force

# evaluate with a covariance overlay
.venv/bin/python scripts/kinetics_eval.py --projects <NAME> \
    --covariance-overlay <file>.yaml run --label <tag> --no-plots --no-latest --no-open

# analytical-vs-finite-difference Jacobian check (the repo's only Jacobian regression test)
printf 'settings:\n  use_finite_difference_jacobians: true\n' > fd.yaml
# run twice, with true and false, and diff kinetics_centroid.txt
```

Overlay schema (`merge_covariance_overlay`): `covariances` (absolute), `covariance_scales`
(multiplicative, for per-robot quantities like `contact_wrench`), `contact_model`,
`contact_model_scales`, `*_per_contact`, and `settings` (top-level scalar switches).

---

## 3. The covariance search (`scripts/kinetics_tune.py`)

Optuna TPE over **17 log-scale dimensions**, anchored on the installed mc_rtc config and spanning a
few decades either side. Two-stage: **phase A** screens on 5 cheap datasets
(`HRP5_MultiContact_2/3`, `KO_TRO2024_RHPS1_1`, `SLIPPAGE_2/3`); the best are promoted to
**phase B** on the full set. Trials run in parallel, each pinned to its own `ROS_DOMAIN_ID`.

Objective (lower better, 0 = parity), over `ln(KO/RI-EKF)` per case:

```python
mean       = Σ ln(ratio) / n
soft_worst = ln( Σ exp(β·ln ratio) / n ) / β        # β = WORST_BETA = 6
objective  = 0.6 · mean + 0.4 · soft_worst          # WORST_WEIGHT = 0.4
```

A failed trial scores `FAILURE_OBJECTIVE = 5.0` (~150x worse than parity) rather than infinity.
`SEED = 20260827`.

Dimensions: contact process (pos xy / pos z / ori rp / ori yaw / force / torque), contact initial
for new contacts (pos, ori), state process (pos / ori / linvel / angvel), gyro bias process,
unmodeled force & torque process, gyro bias initial (xy and z split — z trades against yaw, xy
against tilt; the RI-EKF leaves its b_z untouched because that direction is unobservable).

Excluded on purpose: `contact_wrench` and IMU noise (`SENSOR_CALIBRATION`) — hardware calibration,
and `apply_to_mc_rtc` cannot express them faithfully, so a win found there does not survive
installation.

Installing a result rewrites `~/.config/mc_rtc/observers/MCKineticsObserver.yaml` (a symlink into
`~/devel/src/mc_rtc_configs`) by line-level substitution, so comments survive.

---

## 4. Conventions and traps (each of these has already produced a wrong conclusion)

1. **mc_rtc logs at the END of an iteration.** Row `i` holds the inputs used in iteration `i` *and*
   the state produced by it. `MEKF_initialState_*` is a separate, constant channel holding the true
   pre-run state — that is what the converter restores, correctly.
2. **The logger stores INVERSE quaternions.** `MEKF_estimatedState_ori`,
   `debug_contactKine_*_orientation`, `MocapAligner_worldBodyKine_ori` — all inverted. Comparing
   without inverting gives ~76 deg mean "error" that is pure artefact.
3. **`MEKF_estimatedState_position` is the CENTROID**, not the floating base. The floating base is
   `mcko_fb_posW_*`. They differ by ~200 mm.
4. **`kinetics.txt` already has the time offset applied.** Do not subtract `time_offset.json`
   again; `kinetics_tune.py` correctly does not.
5. **Diff hunk headers name the function at the top of the hunk**, often the *preceding* one.
   Always confirm the enclosing function before attributing a change.
6. **Never read a stripped diff and infer behaviour** — context lines that were not changed can
   invert the meaning. Open the file.
7. **A run is corrupt if `kinetics.txt` has the wrong row count** or any non-monotonic timestamp;
   duplicated messages masquerade as filter divergence (trans 3.5 m, yaw 108 deg). Expected rows:
   LongWalk 1474096, MC_1 11151, MC_2 10249, MC_3 10581, MC_4 10438, RHPS1_1 81792, _2 104897,
   _3 80813, _4 97257, _5 96021, SLIPPAGE_1 20800, _2 22600, _3 21200.
8. **Concurrent runs must use distinct `ROS_DOMAIN_ID`s**, else messages cross-talk into the wrong
   output bag.
9. **`cmake --build . --target install` on state-observation runs `cmake_uninstall.cmake` first.**
   If `CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX` is wrong it deletes the installed library and then fails. It must be
   `/home/arnaud/devel/install`. `/home/arnaud/devel/src/state-observation/build` is a symlink to
   `/home/arnaud/devel/build/state-observation`.
10. **state-observation and mc_state_observation build as Debug** (no `-DNDEBUG`), so
    `BOOST_ASSERT` / `CheckNaN` are live. In RelWithDebInfo a NaN would propagate silently instead.
11. **Contact IDs differ between pipelines.** mc_rtc orders LeftFootCenter=0, RightFootCenter=1;
    the converter assigns from the YAML list order (Right=0). Harmless for the trajectory (3.5 nm,
    both feet configured identically) but the slots do not mean what they say.
12. **Stale duplicate install trees exist** under `catkin_ws/src/install/` and
    `catkin_ws/src/state_observation_ros2/install/`. The live one is `catkin_ws/install/`. Diffing
    against the stale copies produces phantom "version skew".

---

## 5. Verified-correct as of 2026-09-02

- All appendix Jacobians checked against finite differences. **One typo**: `eq:jac_vec_RRR` ends
  `R^T R0^T`, must be `R0^T R^T` (its own intermediate step `eq:jac_vecR_comp` has it right). It
  propagates into `∂T_i/∂φ^R`. **Not yet fixed in the .tex** (owner's choice).
- Both EKF contact-torque implementations (old `Vk`/`Vk2`, new column-wise `J_oriDiff`) are exact.
- `computeAMatrix`/`computeCMatrix` verified end-to-end against the library's own finite-difference
  path: 0.166 um mean over 10438 iterations.
- The **contact-to-contact coupling blocks** of `A` (added recently) are large — `‖F_i<-F_j‖ = 0.349`
  against a self block of `0.361`, i.e. ~97% — and match FD. The old code had them at **zero**, so
  this is the most likely origin of the ~2.5 mm behaviour change between builds.
- **Factor graph `ContactMomentFactor::JTr` had the appendix typo; fixed 2026-09-02** and rebuilt.
  The FG has **zero** `numericalDerivative` calls, which is why it went unnoticed — adding them is
  the highest-value test to write.

---

## 6. Current blocker

**The `state-observation` working tree (uncommitted) cannot tick RHPS1.** All 8 RHPS1 datasets
abort in ~6 s with a NaN assertion (`definitions.hpp:447`, `CheckNaN::checkAssert`, `Matrix3`).
The 4 HRP5P MultiContact sets re-tick fine. RHPS1 was last ticked **Aug 27**, before the Sep-1
rebuild, so these code paths had not been exercised since the working-tree changes.

Backtrace attempts were blocked by mc_rtc infrastructure (ZMQ socket binding under gdb; disabling
the GUI server hits a separate mc_rtc null-pointer bug in `ControllerServer::update_rate`).

**Disk state is currently MIXED and must not be used for a search:**

| | log built with |
|---|---|
| 4 x MultiContact | current library (Sep 2 16:0x) |
| 8 x RHPS1 | old library (Aug 27) |
| LongWalk | old library (Aug 31) |

### Order of work

1. Fix the RHPS1 NaN in the `state-observation` working tree. **Gate on everything else.**
2. Re-prepare all 13 (`scratchpad/redo_all.sh` does this with per-project backup/restore).
3. Sanity gate: analytical-vs-FD on 2 datasets; replay-vs-routine parity on 1.
4. Re-run the covariance search — **as a fresh search, not seeded from the installed values.**
   Those were tuned against an observer whose contact-coupling blocks were zero, and against a
   corrupted mocap reference (see below), so the optimum has almost certainly moved.

### Also outstanding

- `resampleMocapAndExtractPose.py:324` had a lever-arm bug (the rigid-body-to-limb offset was
  rotated by a constant instead of the body's world orientation). **Fixed 2026-09-02**; all 13
  `finalDataCSV.csv` were regenerated after it. It changed LongWalk's ground-truth path length by
  14%, so pre-fix numbers are not comparable.
- `replay_dependencies()` now fingerprints `libstate-observation` and `MCKineticsObserver.so`, so a
  build/log mismatch fails loudly instead of appearing as a small unexplained trajectory difference.
- Open physics question: **both** the KO and the RI-EKF climb 1.2-1.5 m in absolute height over
  LongWalk while pure leg kinematics does not, with 73% of it injected during double support
  (~0.8 mm per gait cycle). Magnitude needs re-measuring on a re-ticked log.
